    "paras": [
     "Eurydactylodes symmetricus, sometimes known commonly as the symmetrical gecko or the large-scaled chameleon gecko, is a species of lizard in the family Diplodactylidae. The species is endemic to Grande Terre in New Caledonia."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitats of E. symmetricus are forest and shrubland, at altitudes of 20–1,050 m (66–3,445 ft)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "E. symmetricus may attain a snout-to-vent length (SVL) of 6 cm (2.4 in)."
    ]
   },
